window.LEARN_CONTENT=window.LEARN_CONTENT||{};window.LEARN_CONTENT["a-9563acffd5862bcd"]={"zh":"<p><a id=\"keep-documentation-up-to-date\"></a></p> <h1 id=\"_1\">根据源代码变更更新文档</h1> <p>利用代码和其它来源自动推进文档更新。</p> <p>使用 Codex 对照源代码变更、公开文档、发布说明和 PR 上下文，然后起草范围明确的文档更新，并附上验证步骤再发布。</p> <p><a id=\"best-for\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_2\">适合哪些情况</h2> <ul> <li>需要跟随频繁变化的行为更新的开发者文档、README、运行手册、示例和迁移说明。</li> <li>维护技术产品文档的团队。</li> </ul> <p><a id=\"skills-plugins\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_3\">技能与插件</h2> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>技能或插件</th> <th>用途</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td><a href=\"https://github.com/openai/plugins/tree/main/plugins/github\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">github（需联网）</a></td> <td>当问题来源涉及 GitHub 时，读取问题、拉取请求、评论、审查讨论和失败检查。</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <p><a id=\"starter-prompt\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_4\">起步提示词</h2> <p>根据源代码变更更新文档</p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">根据以下来源更新 [product/feature] 文档：\n- [this repo/source linked repo] 中已更改的源文件\n- 提及新行为的现有文档页面\n- 下方提供的任何关联问题、PR、发布说明或公开参考资料\n\n然后：\n- 识别哪些内容面向用户\n- 只更新确实需要更改的文档\n- 不要把尚未发布的路线图、私有客户信息或仅限内部的信息写入公开文档\n- 保留现有文档结构、术语和交叉链接\n- 运行与本次更改相匹配的文档检查\n\n定稿前，请总结更改内容、验证过的事项，以及无法依据可信来源证实的说法。\n\n[link release notes or other references here]\n</code></pre> <p><a id=\"related-links\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_5\">关联文档</h2> <ul> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-0310706ee8617b64\">工作流</a></li> </ul> <blockquote> <p>完整文档索引请参阅 <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt（需联网）</a>。在文档页面 URL 末尾添加 <code>.md</code>，即可获取该页面的 Markdown 版本。</p> </blockquote> <p><a id=\"introduction\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_6\">简介</h2> <p>与其等上几周再补文档，不如在源代码变更的同时更新文档。Codex 可以检查变更的代码、测试、发布说明、关联问题和 PR 上下文，然后起草范围明确、符合现有结构的文档更新。</p> <p>这个工作流适用于开发者文档、README 更新、变更日志草稿、迁移说明、运行手册，以及其它需要跟随行为变化而更新的内容。</p> <p><a id=\"how-to-use\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_7\">使用方法</h2> <ol> <li>从你需要记录的变更开始。</li> </ol> <p>分享分支、拉取请求、提交、问题或相关文件。如果文档是公开的，请明确要求不要写入尚未发布的路线图、私有客户信息或仅限内部的信息。</p> <ol> <li>让 Codex 找出受影响的文档。</li> </ol> <p>让它搜索现有文档，查找功能名称、配置项、命令、示例和相关术语。</p> <ol> <li>只修改最小而足够的文档范围。</li> </ol> <p>Codex 应保留现有页面结构、术语、交叉链接和 frontmatter。只需增加一条准确说明、示例或小节时，不要进行大范围重写。</p> <ol> <li>验证更改。</li> </ol> <p>要求 Codex 根据代码库运行合适的格式检查和文档检查，并说明每项面向用户的说法有什么证据支持。</p> <p><a id=\"what-to-give-codex\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_8\">应提供哪些材料</h2> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>来源</th> <th>帮助之处</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td>已更改的代码和测试</td> <td>让 Codex 能依据实际行为起草范围明确的文档更新。</td> </tr> <tr> <td>公开发布说明或产品文档</td> <td>帮助 Codex 使用准确的公开术语、可用性信息和功能状态。</td> </tr> <tr> <td>拉取请求或问题上下文</td> <td>解释变更原因，以及哪些用户可见行为需要记录。</td> </tr> <tr> <td>本地文档检查</td> <td>为发布前的完成标准提供具体依据。</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <p>提供公开发布说明等更多上下文，有助于 Codex 避免写入私密信息或尚未公开的更新。</p> <p><a id=\"make-the-workflow-repeatable\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_9\">让工作流可以重复使用</h2> <p>如果某项约定适用于整个代码库，可以把文档要求写入 <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/codex/agent-configuration/agents-md\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">AGENTS.md（本地尚未收录）</a>。例如：</p> <pre><code class=\"language-md\">## Documentation\n\n- When user-facing behavior changes, check whether docs, examples, or changelogs need updates.\n- Public docs must only include public information or behavior visible in this repo.\n- Preserve existing terminology and frontmatter.\n- Run the docs formatting and build checks before final handoff.\n</code></pre> <p>如果流程包含更多步骤，可以把它整理成<a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/codex/build-skills\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">技能（本地尚未收录）</a>，让未来的 Codex 任务按照相同的来源检查、起草和验证流程执行。关于这种模式的更多信息，请参阅<a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/codex/use-cases/reusable-codex-skills\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">将工作流保存为技能（本地尚未收录）</a>。</p> <p>你也可以<a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/codex/automations#schedule-a-task-inside-a-chat\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">在当前对话中为此工作流安排定时任务</a>（官网章节，需联网） <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/codex/automations/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">本地页面（本地尚未收录）</a>。例如，要求它每周获取关联代码库中的近期拉取请求，并据此更新文档：</p> <p><strong>提示词：</strong></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Schedule a task for the workflow above from this chat. Fetch all the recent PRs in [this repo/linked repo] and update docs based on the changes.\n</code></pre><div class=\"prompt-translation\"><div class=\"prompt-reference-heading\"><strong>提示词中文参考</strong><button class=\"copy-code copy-prompt-translation\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"复制中文参考\">复制中文</button></div><div class=\"prompt-reference-text\">请在这段聊天中为上述工作流安排一项定时任务。获取 [this repo/linked repo] 中最近的所有 PR，并根据这些变更更新文档。</div></div>","en":"<h1 id=\"keep-documentation-up-to-date\">Keep documentation up-to-date</h1> <p>Use code and other sources to automate docs updates.</p> <p>Use Codex to compare source code changes, public docs, release notes, and PR context, then draft focused documentation updates with verification steps before publishing.</p> <h2 id=\"best-for\">Best for</h2> <ul> <li>Developer docs, READMEs, runbooks, examples, and migration notes that need to track behavior that changes frequently.</li> <li>Teams that maintain documentation for a technical product.</li> </ul> <h2 id=\"skills-plugins\">Skills &amp; Plugins</h2> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>Skill or plugin</th> <th>Why use it</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td><a href=\"https://github.com/openai/plugins/tree/main/plugins/github\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">github (online)</a></td> <td>Read issues, pull requests, comments, review threads, and failed checks when GitHub is part of your bug intake.</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <h2 id=\"starter-prompt\">Starter prompt</h2> <p>Update Docs From Source Changes</p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Update the [product/feature] documentation based on the following sources:\n- the changed source files in [this repo/source linked repo]\n- the existing docs pages that mention a new behavior\n- any linked issue, PR, release note, or public reference I provide below\n\nThen:\n- identify what is user-facing\n- update only the docs that need to change\n- keep unpublished roadmap, private customer details, and internal-only context out of public docs\n- preserve the existing docs structure, terminology, and cross-links\n- run the docs checks that fit the change\n\nBefore finalizing, summarize what changed, what you verified, and any claims you could not prove from trusted sources.\n\n[link release notes or other references here]\n</code></pre> <h2 id=\"related-links\">Related links</h2> <ul> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-0310706ee8617b64\">Workflows</a></li> </ul> <blockquote> <p>For the complete documentation index, see <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt (online)</a>. Markdown versions of documentation pages are available by appending <code>.md</code> to the page URL.</p> </blockquote> <h2 id=\"introduction\">Introduction</h2> <p>Documentation is easiest to keep current when it is updated alongside source changes, not weeks later. Codex can inspect changed code, tests, release notes, linked issues, and pull request context, then draft a scoped docs update that matches the existing structure.</p> <p>Use this workflow for developer docs, README updates, changelog drafts, migration notes, runbooks, or anything else that needs to track behavior that changes frequently.</p> <h2 id=\"how-to-use\">How to use</h2> <ol> <li>Start from the change you need to document.</li> </ol> <p>Share the branch, pull request, commit, issue, or files. If the docs are public, say explicitly that unpublished roadmap, private customer details, and internal-only context should stay out.</p> <ol> <li>Ask Codex to map the affected docs.</li> </ol> <p>Have it search existing docs for feature names, config keys, commands, examples, and related terms before drafting.</p> <ol> <li>Update the smallest useful docs surface.</li> </ol> <p>Codex should preserve the current page structure, terminology, cross-links, and frontmatter. It should avoid broad rewrites when a precise note, example, or section update is enough.</p> <ol> <li>Verify the changes.</li> </ol> <p>Ask Codex to run formatting and docs checks that fit the repo, then summarize the evidence behind each user-facing claim.</p> <h2 id=\"what-to-give-codex\">What to give Codex</h2> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>Source</th> <th>Why it helps</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td>Changed code and tests</td> <td>Lets Codex analyze actual behavior to draft focused documentation updates.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Public release notes or product docs</td> <td>Helps Codex match public terminology, availability, and feature status.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Pull request or issue context</td> <td>Explains why the change happened and which user-facing behavior matters.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Local docs checks</td> <td>Gives Codex a concrete definition of done before the docs are published.</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <p>Adding more context such as public release notes lets Codex avoid including private context or updates that are not yet public.</p> <h2 id=\"make-the-workflow-repeatable\">Make the workflow repeatable</h2> <p>For a repo-wide convention, add documentation expectations to <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/codex/agent-configuration/agents-md\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">AGENTS.md (not in this local snapshot)</a>. For example:</p> <pre><code class=\"language-md\">## Documentation\n\n- When user-facing behavior changes, check whether docs, examples, or changelogs need updates.\n- Public docs must only include public information or behavior visible in this repo.\n- Preserve existing terminology and frontmatter.\n- Run the docs formatting and build checks before final handoff.\n</code></pre> <p>If the process has more steps, turn it into a <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/codex/build-skills\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">skill (not in this local snapshot)</a> so future Codex tasks can follow the same source-checking, drafting, and verification loop. See <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/codex/use-cases/reusable-codex-skills\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Save workflows as skills (not in this local snapshot)</a> for more details on this pattern.</p> <p>You can also <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/codex/automations#schedule-a-task-inside-a-chat\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">schedule a task for this workflow from the current chat</a> (official section, online) <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/codex/automations/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Local page (not in this local snapshot)</a>. For example, ask Codex to fetch recent GitHub pull requests and keep the docs current every week:</p> <p><strong>Prompt:</strong></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Schedule a task for the workflow above from this chat. Fetch all the recent PRs in [this repo/linked repo] and update docs based on the changes.\n</code></pre>"};
